      "official_mark_scheme_text": "$ar=54$ and $\\dfrac{a}{1-r}=243$. B1 SOI.\n$\\dfrac{54}{r}=243(1-r)$, leading to $243r^2-243r+54=0$ or $9r^2-9r+2=0$; alternatively $a^2-243a+13122=0$. *M1 Forming a 3-term quadratic in $r$ or $a$ from their second term and $S_\\infty$; allow sign errors.\n$k(3r-2)(3r-1)=0$, or $(a-81)(a-162)=0$. DM1 Solving their 3-term quadratic by factorisation, formula or completing the square; if factorising, factors must reproduce $\\pm$ their $r^2$ coefficient.\n$54\\div(\\text{their }\\frac23)=a$, or $54\\div(\\text{their }81)=r$. DM1 May be implied by final answer.\nTenth term $=81(\\frac23)^9=\\dfrac{512}{243}$. A1 OE; exact. Special case: if B1M1DM0DM1, SC B1 for the correct final answer.\nTotal: 5",
